    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "B-757\nPASSENGER SAFETY INFORMATION\nIf you are sitting in an exit row and you cannot read this card or cannot see well enough to follow these\ninstructions, please tell a crew member.\nSEGURIDAD\nSi usted se encuentra sentado/a en una fila de asientos a la par de una salida u usted no entiende el\nidioma ingles, favor de avisarle a un tripulante.\nFederal Regulations require that persons seated in an exit row be capable of physically opening the exit.\nThese exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push, pull, and maneuver when opening.\nIf you are seated in a designated exit row, you may be called upon to assist the crew in an emergency to\nperform the following:\n- Locate, recognize and operate an emergency exit.\n-\nAssess conditions outside an exit to determine safe egress.\nFollow oral directions and hand signals given by a crew member.\nStow or secure the emergency exit door so it will not impede use of the exit.\nAssess the condition of, activate and stabilize an escape slide to assist others in evacuating.\n- Pass expeditiously through an exit, assess, select, and follow a safe path away from exit.\nNo passenger may be seated in a designated exit row if it is likely they are unable to perform one or more\nof the above functions because:\nPerson lacks sufficient mobility, strength, or dexterity in both arms and hands, and both legs.\nPerson is less than 15 years of age.\nPerson cannot read or understand instructions provided related to emergency evacuation or\nunderstand oral crew commands.\nPerson cannot see or hear well enough to perform one or more of the applicable functions.\nPerson cannot give oral commands to others.\nPerson has other responsibilities such as caring for a small child.\nPerson has a condition that might cause them harm if they perform one or more of the functions.\nIf you are seated adjacent to an emergency exit, cannot or do not wish to assist in an emergency, please\nidentify yourself to a Flight Attendant.",
      "BRACE POSITIONS\nPosicione\nCONDITIONS\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through a\nwindow and check outside\nfor the following:\nSMOKE • FIRE • DEBRIS\nIf thick smoke, fire, metal\ndebris or obstructions are\npresent, redirect passengers\nto omer exits.\nevalue la situacior\nSMOKE\nA\nEXIT\nSORTIE\nFIRE\nFLOTATION\nDEBRIS\n0000\n0000\nEXIT\nSORTIE",
      "SAFETY INFORMATION\nNO SMOKING\nNo fumar\nNO SMOKING\nNo smoking at any\ntime while this\nlight is illuminated\nOXYGEN\nOxigeno\nQuickly!\nSEAT BELTS\nCinturón de Seguridad\nFASTEN SEAT BELT\nselt and\nI while\nOVERHEAD COMPARTMENTS\nDO NOT USE\nOK\nNo use\nB-757\nTAKE OFF/LANDING\nAl salir y aterrizar\nWASO-016B\nREV. 12/1/93"
    ],
